 ## Documentation and support
 
 [Bonfÿre system guides](https://docs.aurekai.work/) cover the platform more broadly. The working routes above are the best starting point for evaluating what an operator or buyer can do today.
+
+
+### Brief Studio workspace
+
+The studio now separates opportunities and their working views: brief, checks, routes, source and recipient preview. Each opportunity retains its own recipient, recommendation, formatted memo, budget, comparison mode and included sections. Existing IndexedDB drafts migrate when opened; drafts stay specific to the browser origin. A save compares the stored revision and refuses stale tab writes.
+
+The route matrix shows proposed check coverage. Providers can be excluded from a comparison, edited or added through an eligible-check picker. Estimates and recorded-ready quotes remain separate. Price changes update the same selected-route solution used by the recipient brief and typed proposal.
+
+The reviewer memo uses self-hosted Tiptap 3.32.0 with formatting, undo/redo and source links. A bounded document schema drives HTML and Markdown export. If the editor cannot load, a plain text field remains available; Retry restores the rich editor with those edits.
+
+To rebuild the vendored editor, run `npm ci --ignore-scripts --no-audit --no-fund` in `tools/brief-editor-build`, then `bun build.mjs`. The package lock, bundled licenses and generated provenance record are retained with the source. Publishing `site/` needs no runtime npm installation or external script service.
+
+The current upgrade is published at [the separate preview](https://brief-studio-upgrade.aurekai-work-samples.pages.dev/brief-studio/). GitHub Pages remains on its committed version. Shared account storage, organization permissions and native approval/dispatch are not connected to this browser workspace. Google Stitch design generation remains pending.
